---
import Page from '../layouts/Page.astro';
import { LINKS } from '../consts';

const stack = [
	['Identity', 'Okta, Microsoft Entra ID, MFA, user lifecycle'],
	['Endpoints', 'Microsoft Intune, Kandji, Apple Business Manager, Windows and macOS fleets'],
	['Productivity', 'Microsoft 365, Google Workspace'],
	['Security', 'CrowdStrike'],
	['Service', 'Jira Service Management, Confluence'],
];
---

<Page title="About" description="Giovanni Hale — systems administrator focused on identity, endpoints, and security.">
	<p class="label">About</p>
	<h1>Giovanni Hale</h1>
	<div class="prose">
		<p class="lede">
			I'm a systems administrator. I like being handed an unfamiliar system, figuring out how it
			actually works, and then explaining it clearly to the people who depend on it.
		</p>
		<p>
			I've spent more than ten years in enterprise IT, much of it supporting executives and working
			across identity, endpoint management, and security tooling. That's work where the details
			matter and the person on the other end needs a straight answer, not a lecture.
		</p>
		<p>
			I write these notes for two reasons. Writing is how I make sure I understand something. And
			if you're deciding whether to work with me, I'd rather show you how I think than tell you.
		</p>

		<h2>What I've worked with</h2>
		<table>
			<tbody>
				{
					stack.map(([area, tools]) => (
						<tr>
							<th scope="row">{area}</th>
							<td>{tools}</td>
						</tr>
					))
				}
			</tbody>
		</table>

		<h2>Background</h2>
		<p>
			B.S. in Information Technology, cybersecurity concentration. Before IT, I served as a U.S. Navy
			Hospital Corpsman.
		</p>

		<h2>Elsewhere</h2>
		<p>
			<a href={LINKS.github}>GitHub</a> · <a href={LINKS.youtube}>YouTube</a>
		</p>
	</div>
</Page>

<style>
	th {
		width: 8.5rem;
	}
</style>
